    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "df3967d1_1c7218ae",
        "filename": "keystone/common/api_version_request.py",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 16465
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-03T18:34:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could theoretically have more than one deprecated version. This limits us in that regard. I would argue that this should be a list of dictionaries. Where dictionaries have keys for \u0027version\u0027 and \u0027last_updated\u0027.",
      "revId": "e4342171921be823d9aa7d01819d3a1ff447fedd",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "df3967d1_7c8b641e",
        "filename": "keystone/common/api_version_request.py",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 16465
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-03T18:34:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I feel strongly about not dividing the version information into multiple files and methods which is what we\u0027re doing here. Put all of these in a dictionary with the version as the key. So you have VERSIONS \u003d { \u0027v3\u0027: { \u0027status\u0027: \u0027stable\u0027, \u0027last_updated\u0027: date }, \u0027v2\u0027: {...} }. Have a list for DEPRECATED_VERSIONS \u003d [\u0027v2.0\u0027] where v2.0 is the key in the VERSIONS dictionary.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 44,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 46,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "e4342171921be823d9aa7d01819d3a1ff447fedd",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
